7.3 adjustments:
- Pass the reclaim swap_io_ctx through. When kcompressd has no caller
  context it uses a private one and swap_write_submit()s it, so a bio
  cannot be left on the stack. Overflow writeback uses the reclaim
  context and is submitted with the rest of the shrink batch.
- Sample folio_memcg() under rcu_read_lock(); 7.3 requires that.
- Hold kcompress_fifo_lock across dequeue and enqueue. kcompressd runs
  with PF_KSWAPD and can re-enter the queue path, so there is more than
  one writer. A single-producer kfifo_in() would race.
- Wait with kthread_should_stop() in the condition, drain the fifo on
  the way out, and mark the thread freezable. Otherwise kswapd_stop()
  can sleep forever in kthread_stop(), and suspend can race swap IO.

